 boundary: "ACL2 owns which peers and when (fn-pull-schedule, fn-sched-pull-*), every byte sent, every reply meaning, the 600 s round deadline (fn-prd-round-seconds books/peer-round-driver.lisp:59), the 512-octet controller windows and when the cursor moves. Host dials, moves octets, runs the spool worker thread (host/native/catchup-spool.lisp:84) and appends+fsyncs FNPL/FNCU cursor frames (fnn-pull-journal-append host/native/pull-service.lisp:233; a failed append is fnn-indeterminate, never a refusal). A catch-up cursor frame is appended only at batch end (fn-cu-next books/peer-catchup.lisp:272) after the whole batch was replayed to the local node by IHAVE, so a cut resumes at the last batch boundary and re-offered duplicates answer 435. A bank lease settles only after the spool worker thread is joined clean, the socket is shut and the local transit connection is closed; a cleanup fault keeps the lease held (host/native/pull-service.lisp:942 to host/native/pull-service.lisp:972). The local node answers through the owner transit connection (fn-owner-open-peer via fnn-pull-local-open host/native/pull-service.lisp:272)."
