 boundary: "ACL2 decides publication due-ness (fn-ock-publication-next), the estimate / defer / plan verdict before any allocation (fn-ockp-decide), every frame, every cut outcome (fn-orcp-cut-outcome) and the swap word. Host holds the arena pin, writes through the publication buffer in bounded steps, fsyncs, renames and drops covered segments. A failure before the rename is a known failure (old checkpoint stays, stage removed); at or after it the outcome is fnn-indeterminate (host/native/io.lisp:3172). The staged file is read back and verified before the rename, so the segment drop never follows an unreadable file (host/native/io.lisp:3031). At most one publication is in flight and a reclaim pass is the publication in flight (fn-owner-sco-publication-done releases only its own slot). Dropped-segment blocks return through fnn-owner-release-extents only after generation-pin checks. Doc drift: books/reclaim-cuts.lisp:14 says :interned means the tombstones were interned into the live arena, but the host reaches :interned (host/native/owner.lisp:7998) after PREDICTING them and seals only in the swap quantum (host/native/owner.lisp:8047). The requested sequence capture > rewrite > stage > predict > install > swap > release maps to cuts captured, rewritten, staged, (predict then) interned, (rebuilt), installed, swapped, released."
 coverage: "READ IN FULL: host/native/checkpoint.lisp (1-514), books/byte-store-state-checkpoint-program.lisp, host/checkpoint-host.lisp head, host/native/io.lisp 2700-3330 (plan, load, stage, verify, install, test faults) and 3500-3960 (batch constants, yield, walk, arena steps, history image, write-steps, publish-steps), host/native/owner.lisp 6960-7420 (snapshot jobs, publisher, publish-captured, maybe-publish) and 7680-8220 (reclaim cuts, install-stobj, reclaim pass). READ IN PART: host/owner-host.lisp 760-830, 885-960, 1020-1075, 5395-5560; books/owner-reclaim-pass.lisp 1-80, 140-235, 296-320, 440-460; books/owner-checkpoint-open.lisp 90-120, 200-330; books/checkpoint-auxiliary.lisp 60-146; books/reclaim-cuts.lisp 1-25. SKIMMED or grep only: books/checkpoint-codec.lisp, books/checkpoint-compaction.lisp, books/checkpoint-publish.lisp, books/checkpoint-reserve.lisp, books/store-checkpoint-*.lisp, books/owner-checkpoint-pipeline.lisp, books/owner-checkpoint-writer.lisp, books/reclaim-chunked-*.lisp. NOT READ: fnn-log-rotate / fnn-log-drop / fnn-log-covered-indices bodies (host/native/io.lisp:8201-8400), fnn-owner-release-extents body, fnn-owner-reclaim-dry-run body, fnn-recover-log-from-log-checkpoint, fnn-open-live-store. Nothing here was executed or tested."
