 keystone: "ACK VS DURABLE ACCEPTANCE: fn-tcl-delivery-plan-decides-exactly-by-the-held-final-ack-and-the-callback (books/tcpcl-delivery.lisp:111; PRF-1036 certified), fn-tcl-late-refusal-gets-no-final-ack (books/tcpcl-delivery-invariants.lisp:187), fn-tcl-uncertain-delivery-withholds-final-ack (books/tcpcl-delivery-invariants.lisp:207), fn-tcl-acknowledged-custody-is-progressed-in-its-turn (books/tcpcl-delivery-invariants.lisp:263; PRF-906), fn-tcl-host-drive-bundle-has-held-final (books/tcpcl-delivery-invariants.lisp:149; PRF-060). CHANNEL: fn-bpaj-refused-channel-takes-no-custody (books/bp-channel-ingress.lisp:175), fn-bpaj-admitted-channel-receives-under-its-ingress (books/bp-channel-ingress.lisp:201) (PRF-128). GRANT CUSTODY: fn-bpsg-physical-alone-cannot-settle-context (books/bp-session-profile.lisp:93), fn-bpsp-startup-hold-protects-baseline-and-all-contexts (books/bp-session-profile.lisp:88), fn-bpsg-acquire-turn-selected-draw-correspondence (books/resource-bp-session.lisp:105); PRF-1276, PRF-1291, PRF-1296 and PRF-1309 are status planned in planning/proofs.json. NONE FOUND for: the converse (a logical receipt alone cannot settle), the composed host boundary of fnn-bp-session-abort-all (PRF-1296 names only a definition-expansion helper, books/bp-session-profile.lisp:143), passive admission before source installation (PRF-1299 planned, no events), and loop-level fairness or liveness of fnn-bp-session-loop. books/bp-adu.lisp and books/bp-workflow.lisp hold no keystone for the session (codec and workflow decisions)."
 boundary: "ACL2 decides every protocol message, every delivery status and refusal reason, admission of the channel and the announced EID, the custody settle word and the receipt rule; host owns the socket, the single writer loop, the durability barriers and the held ACK queue. Transport ACK is distinct from durable acceptance: the final END ACK stays in fnn-tclc-held until fn-tcl-delivery-plan releases it, for (:accepted) only. A grant settles only after BOTH an affirmative physical close receipt (fnn-socket-shut :closed) and a logical context-release receipt; an unobserved close keeps custody and cannot be retried (host/native/bp-session.lisp:81). Volatile private source aliases are retired only in pre-publication phases (fn-bpsrx-abort-plan books/bp-session-received-source.lisp:41); publishing, fenced or foreign contexts retain authority. Funding is a staged projection, not a complete allocator/GC/decode tariff (PRF-1276 scope text)."
 coverage: "READ IN FULL: host/native/bp-session.lisp (1-412), books/resource-bp-session.lisp, books/bp-session-profile.lisp 44-146, books/bp-session-received-source.lisp. READ IN PART: host/native/bp-node.lisp 930-1260 (forward start, passive begin, receipt turn, fnn-command-bp-node), host/native/bp-service.lisp 1-56, 100-135, 1124-1430, host/native/tcpcl.lisp 1-90, 150-180, 292-360, 460-800 (stage, flush, drop, settle-delivery, act, apply, offer, begin, turn), books/tcpcl-delivery.lisp 40-125, books/bp-channel-ingress.lisp 150-240, books/bp-node-receive-boundary.lisp 130-175, books/bp-node-profile-admission.lisp 40-70, books/bp-session-scheduler.lisp 1-40, host/native/bp.lisp 554-570. SKIMMED or grep only: books/tcpcl-session.lisp, books/tcpcl-records.lisp, books/tcpcl-retained-turn.lisp, books/tcpcl-source-*.lisp, books/bp-node-foundation.lisp, host/native/bp-service.lisp 202-1123 (persist and drive-effect bodies), books/bp-adu.lisp, books/bp-workflow.lisp, books/bp-receive-evidence.lisp, host/native/tcpcl.lisp 90-150, 180-292, 360-460 (input and materialize turns), 800-1023 (CLI). NOT TRACED: fnn-bplc listener set, fnn-bpnc control pump, fnn-bpnode-dispatch-one, fnn-bps-drive-effect arms. Nothing here was executed or tested."
